{
  "sn42.8:0.1": "Linked Discourses 42.8 ",
  "sn42.8:0.2": "1. Chiefs ",
  "sn42.8:0.3": "A Horn Blower ",
  "sn42.8:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Nāḷandā in Pāvārika’s Mango Grove. ",
  "sn42.8:1.2": "Then Asibandhaka’s son the chief, who was a disciple of the Jains, went up to the Buddha, and sat down to one side. The Buddha said to him, ",
  "sn42.8:1.3": "“Chief, how does the Jain ascetic of the Ñātika clan teach his disciples?” ",
  "sn42.8:1.4": "“Sir, this is how the Jain Ñātika teaches his disciples: ",
  "sn42.8:1.5": "‘Everyone who kills a living creature, steals, commits sexual misconduct, or lies goes to a place of loss, to hell. ",
  "sn42.8:1.6": "You’re led on by what you frequently live by.’ ",
  "sn42.8:1.7": "This is how the Jain Ñātika teaches his disciples.” ",
  "sn42.8:1.8": "“‘You’re led on by what you usually live by’: if this were true, then, according to what the Jain Ñātika says, no one would go to a place of loss, to hell. ",
  "sn42.8:2.1": "What do you think, chief? ",
  "sn42.8:2.2": "Take a person who kills living creatures. If we compare periods of time during the day and night, which is more frequent: the occasions when they’re killing or when they’re not killing?” ",
  "sn42.8:2.3": "“The occasions when they’re killing are less frequent, while the occasions when they’re not killing are more frequent.” ",
  "sn42.8:2.4": "“‘You’re led on by what you usually live by’: if this were true, then, accord